This is a nice theory, but in practice I've very rarely felt
constrained by the number of skill slots available and I've rarely
watched another regular ascender's game where it looked like a major
issue.  It happens occasionally for spellcasters who find a good
assortment of low-level spells very early on, but it's hardly a major
constraint even there.

(And surviving the early game is a lot tougher than the late game, if
you can make a tradeoff that helps the former significantly it's
almost always worth it unless it makes the late game much, much harder
indeed.)


